  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1250 AM CDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nThe upper ridge will remain centered over the Plain through \nFriday but will begin shifting eastward by Saturday, as an upper \nlevel trough approaches from the west. Warm temperatures will \ncontinue, with highs Thursday and Friday in the low to mid 80s, \nwith overnight lows in the 50s and lower 60s. \n\nThe upper trough will gradually move east across the Plains by\nearly next week. Ahead of the trough, moisture will increase over\nthe weekend, with an increase in cloud cover and slightly cooler\ntemperatures. Rain chances will begin to increase across the area\nas early as Sunday afternoon and evening across far western \ncounties, but the better chance for showers and a few storms will\nbe Monday and Monday night, as a cold front moves in from the \nnorth. Model blends maintain low to medium chance rain chances \n(20%-40%) by this time, with rain chances tapering off on \nTuesday. There is still some uncertainty regarding the evolution \nand timing of this system, and additional forecast changes are \nlikely as we head towards the weekend. In addition to the rain \nchances, cooler temperatures will return to the area, with highs \nin the 70s from Sunday through Tuesday.",
